Online since 12.11.2026 Share on URL copied in the clipboard! Entry into office: 1 July 2027 Take your first professional steps in a state-of-the-art clinic, serving people who learn to live after an accident. Join the Romance Rehabilitation Clinic (CRR) in Sion as: MP-E Intern Professional Maturity Economics and Services (MP-E) What are we doing? At the RRC, we accompany people who have experienced an accident or have neurological disorders (para- or tetraplegia, amputation, burns, stroke, head injury) to regain their autonomy and, where possible, their place in working life. For more information: www.crr-suva.ch. Your internship in brief
• Duration: 12 months
• Activity rate: 100%
• Location: Sion
• Start: July 1, 2027
• Planned tours include HR, administration and patient flow management Your missions Depending on the department, you can, for example:
• receive and guide patients and visitors;
• preparing, entering and classifying files and data;
• process mail, orders and billing;
• participate in the planning and organisation of the daily lives of the teams;
• support HR service (staff files, contracts, recruitment). Your profile
• You're in MP-E training or you're about to start it;
• You are curious, comfortable in contact with others and benevolent;
• You are reliable, punctual, precise and have a sense of responsibility;
• You're as comfortable behind a screen as you are face to face;
• You want to integrate the world of health and be part of our mission. What we offer
• A concrete and rewarding immersion on the ground;
• The discovery of several domains thanks to the tournus;
• Various missions that develop your administrative and organizational skills;
• An accompaniment structured by a trainer throughout your internship. Our benefits
• Remuneration above market standards;
• Low-cost meals;
• Free access to sports facilities and swimming pool;
• Time dedicated to your studies to suit your manager;
• The ability to continue your career at the CRA after your SFA, depending on the positions available. Want to apply? If the world of health resonates in you and you want to join a team that will support you throughout your internship, apply to us!
• Send us your complete file (motivation letter, CV, copy of the latest notes) via the form below;
• Deadline: 06.12.2026
• Start of internship: 1 July 2027. Your contact Jennifer Jean , Specialized HR Assistant: 027 603 30 26 Apply Now Cookie Statement By continuing your navigation on this site, you accept the use of cookies to improve your user experience and to realize visits' statistics. You can customize the use of cookies using the button below. Accept all Refuse All My Preferences

