Online since 12.11.2026 Share on URL copied in the clipboard! Started: 1 August 2027 Looking for a rewarding experience? Integrate our clinic specializing in the advanced rehabilitation and reintegration of accident victims in Sion, and join our team at the technical foot orthopaedic workshop as: Apprenti·e Bottier/Ere-Orthopedist CFC What are we doing? Each of us at the RRC is committed to supporting patients to become actors in their lives again. We help those who have experienced an accident or have neurological disorders to regain their autonomy and, where possible, to return to work. We are there to meet specific rehabilitation needs: in para or tetraplegic people, amputated, burned or after a stroke or head injury. To learn more about our clinic, visit our website www.crr-suva.ch/ Your main missions
• You adapt and repair standard shoes;
• You make tailor-made soles and orthotics;
• You make test shoes to test and adjust;
• You welcome patients to understand their needs according to their medical prescription;
• You mount final shoes: cutting, assembly, sewing, bonding;
• You take prints from your feet and create a custom mold. What you bring to the team
• Your attraction and skill for manual tasks;
• Your investment and collaboration in helping patients;
• Your sense of curiosity, relationship, your commitment and your benevolence;
• Your desire to integrate the world of health and be part of our mission. What we expect from you We rely on you to be involved both in your training and in the field. Dynamism, sense of responsibility, precision and learning will be the key words of your journey, not to mention attendance and punctuality that define you fully! What we offer
• Various missions combining manual know-how, technology and human contact;
• A structured accompaniment throughout your learning. Our benefits
• Remuneration above market standards;
• Low-cost meals;
• Free access to sports facilities and swimming pool;
• Time dedicated to your studies to suit your manager.
• The ability to continue your career at the CRA after your SFA, depending on the positions available. Want to apply? If the world of health resonates in you and you want to join a team that will support you throughout your internship, apply to us!
• Send us your complete file (motivation letter, CV, copy of the latest transcripts and/or internship report) via the form available below,
• Deadline: 6 December 2026,
• Entry into office: 1 August 2027. Your contacts Yannick Tellier , Head of the Technical Foot Orthopaedics Workshop, at 027 603 24 45 Jennifer Jean , Specialized HR Assistant, at 027 603 30 26 Apply Now Cookie Statement By continuing your navigation on this site, you accept the use of cookies to improve your user experience and to realize visits' statistics. You can customize the use of cookies using the button below. Accept all Refuse All My Preferences

